abstract: >-
  An open book of executed Jupyter notebooks, with a small Python module, on
  the Onsager variational principle in soft matter: the Rayleighian, Onsager's
  kinetic equations and reciprocal relations, how to write free energies and
  dissipation functions, the derivation of the diffusion, Stokes and Darcy
  equations, the approximation method with trial functions, and their first
  applications to liquids and interfaces (capillary rise and imbibition;
  spreading of a droplet; coalescence and sintering; a drying droplet) and to
  soft materials (diffusion and sedimentation of colloids; swelling and
  squeezing of a gel; phase separation; polymer dynamics; nematic liquid
  crystals). Every variational result is checked against an exact or
  numerical solution.
